<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
 "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Footswitch needs no special entitlements under the hardened runtime.

    The app installs a CGEvent tap and synthesizes keystrokes; on macOS those
    capabilities are gated by the Accessibility TCC permission the user grants
    at runtime (System Settings -> Privacy & Security -> Accessibility), NOT by
    a code-signing entitlement. The app is not sandboxed, has no network use,
    and reads/writes only ~/.footswitch which it owns.

    This file exists so the signing command is uniform and any future
    entitlement has an obvious home. An empty dict is valid and intentional.
  -->
</dict>
</plist>
